<title>USA: Mass. Gov Weld submits bill to eliminate counties.</title>
<headline>Mass. Gov Weld submits bill to eliminate counties.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Massachusetts Gov William Weld on Tuesday said he filed a bill to eliminate the 300-year-old system of county government, transferring their essential functions to the state as of July 1, 1998.</p>
<p>&quot;Taxpayers will no longer support this layer of inefficient and burdensome bureaucracy,&quot; Weld said in a statement.</p>
</text>
